title:: BMMIDICCController
summary:: Documentation BEASTmulch - Generic MIDI Control Change Controller	
categories:: Classes

Description::

This class implements a generic controller which receives MIDI control change messages.

See also: link::Classes/Root Classes/BMAbstractController::, link::Classes/Controllers/BMAbstractMIDIController::, link::Classes/Controllers/BMMIDIBendController::

CLASSMETHODS::

method:: new
Create a new BMMIDICCController.

argument:: midiport
An instance of link::Classes/Inputs and Outputs/BMMIDIPort::.
argument:: name
A Symbol indicating the name of this controller.
argument:: chan
The MIDI Channel to receive on. Note these start from 0.
argument:: ccArray
An Array of Integers indicating which control numbers constitute this object's controls, and the order in which they should occur.
argument:: server
An instance of Server. If you pass nil this will be the default Server.
	
code::	
// initialise MIDI ports
BMMIDIPort.init;
// get a port
p = BMMIDIPort.ports['IAC Bus 1'];
b = BMMIDICCController.new(p, \bendController, 0, [7, 1], s); // volume and mod
	
b.free; // free my resources
::

method:: newFromParamDict
Create a new instance using a parameter dictionary. (See link::Classes/Root Classes/BMAbstractController:: for more information.)

argument:: dict
A Dictionary or subclass with values for the following keys: code::\midiport:: -> An instance of link::Classes/Inputs and Outputs/BMMIDIPort::, code::\chan:: -> An Integer from 0 to 15, code::\ccArray:: -> An Int8Array, name -> A Symbol indicating the name of this controller.
argument:: server
An instance of Server. If you pass nil this will be the default Server.


